.TH BIGFLOATZERO 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatInit, bigFloatDestroy, bigFloatZero, bigFloatCopy, bigFloatSwap, bigFloatFromUint32 \- manage dynamic binary floats
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

void bigFloatInit(BigFloat *x);
void bigFloatDestroy(BigFloat *x);
void bigFloatZero(BigFloat *x);
int bigFloatCopy(BigFloat *dst, const BigFloat *src);
void bigFloatSwap(BigFloat *a, BigFloat *b);
int bigFloatFromUint32(BigFloat *x, uint32_t v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Init creates a fresh allocation-free positive zero with default precision
1024 limbs. BIGFLOAT_INIT is equivalent. Destroy frees the mantissa and restores
that initial state. Zero retains capacity and precision while setting positive
zero. Never initialize a live allocation again without destroying it.
.PP
Copy deep-copies value, sign, exponent and precision into an initialized
destination. Self-copy is supported. Swap exchanges ownership and metadata.
FromUint32 sets and normalizes a scalar using the existing precision.
Structure assignment is not a deep copy. Destroy every initialized object
when finished, including on error paths.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Init, Destroy, Zero and Swap return void. Copy and FromUint32 return 0,
-1 for allocation failure, INT_MAX for size/exponent range failure, or -2 for
an invalid zero precision. Errors leave the destination unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
